  "mf-auto-202": "Routine Maintenance",
  "mf-auto-203": "Collet Cleaning",
  "mf-auto-204": "Routine Maintenance",
  "mf-auto-205": "The collet is a key component that significantly affects machining accuracy. Inspect and clean it regularly.",
  "mf-auto-206": "When cleaning the inside of the equipment, make sure zirconia dust, PMMA dust, or other foreign matter does not remain inside the collet.",
  "mf-auto-207": "The collet is a consumable part. Periodic replacement is recommended. (Expected collet life: approx.",
  "mf-auto-208": "100,000 minutes)",
  "mf-auto-209": "Reference",
  "mf-auto-210": "Collet life may vary depending on the user's machining material, machining method, and usage environment.",
  "mf-auto-211": "If the equipment is powered off for more than 24 hours, store it with a tool or collet pin inserted inside the collet.",
  "mf-auto-212": "Be sure to use genuine tools.",
  "mf-auto-213": "Caution",
  "mf-auto-214": "When cleaning or maintaining the collet, be careful not to scratch the inside or outside of the collet.",
  "mf-auto-215": "Also, do not apply excessive force that could deform the collet.",
  "mf-auto-216": "Recommended Cleaning Cycle",
  "mf-auto-217": "Clean the collet regularly. At least",
  "mf-auto-218": "once a week",
  "mf-auto-219": "is recommended.",
  "mf-auto-220": "1. Move the spindle position",
  "mf-auto-221": "Move the spindle to a position that is easy to work in.",
  "mf-auto-222": "If necessary,",
  "mf-auto-223": "Jog Mode",
  "mf-auto-224": "can be used.",
  "mf-auto-225": "Secure work space",
  "mf-auto-226": "Secure enough space below the spindle to remove and clean the collet.",
  "mf-auto-227": "2. Open the collet",
  "mf-auto-228": "Open the collet in the control program.",
  "mf-auto-229": "3. Remove the collet",
  "mf-auto-230": "Insert the collet pin into the collet and attach the collet adapter to the collet.",
  "mf-auto-231": "If you do not have a collet pin, a broken tool can be used as a substitute.",
  "mf-auto-232": "With the collet pin or broken tool inserted, use the torque driver to turn the collet",
  "mf-auto-233": "clockwise",
  "mf-auto-234": "to remove it from the spindle.",
  "mf-auto-235": "5. Clean the collet",
  "mf-auto-236": "If a steam cleaner is available, spray the inside and outside of the collet to remove foreign matter.",
  "mf-auto-237": "Then use the",
  "mf-auto-238": "collet cleaning brush",
  "mf-auto-239": "included in the starter kit to clean the collet.",
  "mf-auto-240": "Cleaning Check",
  "mf-auto-241": "Carefully check that no dust or foreign matter remains in the collet gaps.",
  "mf-auto-242": "6. Apply grease",
  "mf-auto-243": "After cleaning, apply a thin layer of grease to the collet surface.",
  "mf-auto-244": "Do not apply excessive grease.",
  "mf-auto-245": "Excessive grease can attract dust and cause collet contamination.",
  "mf-auto-246": "7. Prepare to install the collet",
  "mf-auto-247": "With the collet pin or broken tool inserted into the collet, attach the collet adapter and torque driver together.",
  "mf-auto-248": "Set the torque driver to the",
  "mf-auto-249": "specified range.",
  "mf-auto-250": "If a torque driver is not available,",
  "mf-auto-251": "use a 0.6 N m torque adapter",
  "mf-auto-252": ".",
  "mf-auto-253": "8. Install the collet",
  "mf-auto-254": "Insert the collet into the spindle, then turn it",
  "mf-auto-255": "counterclockwise",
  "mf-auto-256": "to secure it.",
  "mf-auto-257": "Confirm that the collet is fully fastened.",
  "mf-auto-258": "9. Close the collet",
  "mf-auto-259": "Close the collet in the control program.",
  "mf-auto-260": "10. Final check",
  "mf-auto-261": "After collet cleaning and installation are complete, check the following items.",
  "mf-auto-262": "Confirm that the collet is correctly fastened to the spindle.",
  "mf-auto-263": "Confirm that no foreign matter remains inside the collet.",
  "mf-auto-264": "Confirm that no excessive grease remains on the collet surface.",
  "mf-auto-265": "Confirm that tools can be inserted and held normally.",
